INSERT INTO d VALUES (1, 10_000_000_000_000_000::DATE), (2, '2024-01-01'::DATE);
SELECT k, v, v::TIMESTAMP FROM d;
SELECT k FROM d WHERE v > '2000-01-01T00:00:00.000000Z'::TIMESTAMP;
```

Actual: row 1 (`318857-05-20T17:46:40.000Z`) converts to `-265697-05-04T09:44:50.448384Z`, so the WHERE returns only row 2.
Expected: an error (or NULL), never a different valid timestamp. The test expects the error that `'2300-01-01'::TIMESTAMP::TIMESTAMP_NS` already gives.

Also: DATE to TIMESTAMP_NS wraps from year 2263 (`'2300-01-01'::DATE::TIMESTAMP_NS` gives year 1715). Related: #7389.

Likely cause: `MicrosTimestampDriver.fromDate` and `NanosTimestampDriver.fromDate` multiply without an overflow check.

Reproduced on master 6c63556431.

