FILL(LINEAR) returns NULL instead of the interpolated value when the DOUBLE values are large (above about 5E298 with 1h buckets), even when both neighbours are equal.

### To reproduce

```sql
CREATE TABLE g (d DOUBLE, ts TIMESTAMP) TIMESTAMP(ts);
INSERT INTO g VALUES (1.0E300, '2024-01-01T00:00:00.000000Z'), (1.0E300, '2024-01-01T02:00:00.000000Z');
SELECT ts, last(d) d FROM g SAMPLE BY 1h FILL(LINEAR);
```

Actual: the 01:00 bucket is `null`.
Expected: `1.0E300`.

Likely cause: `InterpolationUtil.interpolate` computes `(y1 * (x2 - x) + y2 * (x - x1)) / (x2 - x1)` with x in microseconds, so the products overflow before the division. The limit falls as buckets get wider.

Reproduced on master 6c63556431.

