body_text:
QuestDB treats NaN and +/-Infinity in DOUBLE and FLOAT columns as NULL: `WHERE v IS NULL` selects them. But `CASE WHEN v IS NULL` answers "not null" for the infinities, so one query disagrees with itself.

### To reproduce

Infinity can only be written over ILP (SQL arithmetic gives NaN):

```
inf_t k=1i,v=Infinity
inf_t k=2i,v=-Infinity
inf_t k=3i,v=1.5
```

```sql
SELECT k, CASE WHEN v IS NULL THEN 'is_null' ELSE 'not_null' END c FROM inf_t WHERE v IS NULL;
```

Actual: rows 1 and 2, labelled `not_null`.
Expected: `is_null`.

Also: `CASE v WHEN NULL` and `CASE WHEN v = NULL`; FLOAT the same. Related: #5926.

Likely cause: this CASE becomes a switch that matches DOUBLE keys by their bits, so only NaN reaches the NULL branch.

Reproduced on master 6c63556431.

<details>
<summary>Failing test</summary>

Add to `core/src/test/java/io/questdb/test/griffin/engine/functions/conditional/SwitchFunctionFactoryTest.java`:

```java
@Test
public void testDoubleIsNullTreatsInfinityAsNull() throws Exception {
    assertMemoryLeak(() -> {
        // SQL turns every non-finite DOUBLE into NaN; the table writer keeps an infinity as it is
        execute("CREATE TABLE t (k INT, v DOUBLE)");
        try (TableWriter w = getWriter("t")) {
            TableWriter.Row r = w.newRow();
            r.putInt(0, 1);
            r.putDouble(1, Double.POSITIVE_INFINITY);
            r.append();
            r = w.newRow();
            r.putInt(0, 2);
            r.putDouble(1, Double.NEGATIVE_INFINITY);
            r.append();
            r = w.newRow();
            r.putInt(0, 3);
            r.putDouble(1, 1.5);
            r.append();
            w.commit();
        }
        // WHERE v IS NULL selects the infinities; the CASE, which the parser rewrites into a
        // switch, must agree with it
        assertQuery("SELECT k, CASE WHEN v IS NULL THEN 'is_null' ELSE 'not_null' END c FROM t WHERE v IS NULL")
                .noLeakCheck()
                .returns("""
                        k\tc
                        1\tis_null
                        2\tis_null
                        """);
    });
}
```

On master it fails with: `AssertionError: expected:<k\tc\n1\tis_null\n2\tis_null> but was:<k\tc\n1\tnot_null\n2\tnot_null>`

</details>

