body_text:
A fill list that mixes LINEAR with another fill mode fails with a NullPointerException when TO reaches past the last row.

### To reproduce

```sql
CREATE TABLE t (x DOUBLE, y DOUBLE, ts TIMESTAMP) TIMESTAMP(ts);
INSERT INTO t VALUES (1.0, 10.0, '2024-01-01T01:00:00.000000Z'), (2.0, 20.0, '2024-01-01T02:00:00.000000Z');
SELECT ts, avg(x) x, avg(y) y FROM t
SAMPLE BY 1h FROM '2024-01-01T01:00:00.000000Z' TO '2024-01-01T05:00:00.000000Z'
FILL(LINEAR, NULL);
```

Actual: `NullPointerException: Cannot invoke "io.questdb.cairo.sql.Record.getDouble(int)" because "rec" is null`
Expected: four rows, with 03:00 and 04:00 NULL in both columns, as `FILL(NULL, NULL)` gives.

Also: `FILL(NULL, LINEAR)` and `FILL(LINEAR, 7)`. With a gap before the last row, the trailing rows are dropped instead, which is #7797.

Reproduced on master 6c63556431.

<details>
<summary>Failing test</summary>

Add to `core/src/test/java/io/questdb/test/griffin/engine/groupby/SampleByTest.java`:

```java
@Test
public void testSampleByFromToFillLinearAndNull() throws Exception {
    assertMemoryLeak(() -> {
        execute("CREATE TABLE t (x DOUBLE, y DOUBLE, ts TIMESTAMP) TIMESTAMP(ts) PARTITION BY DAY BYPASS WAL");
        execute("INSERT INTO t VALUES (1.0, 10.0, '2024-01-01T01:00:00.000000Z'), (2.0, 20.0, '2024-01-01T02:00:00.000000Z')");
        // the buckets after the last row have no right-hand point to interpolate to,
        // so LINEAR leaves them NULL, as it does for the buckets before the first row
        assertQuery("""
                SELECT ts, avg(x) x, avg(y) y FROM t
                SAMPLE BY 1h FROM '2024-01-01T01:00:00.000000Z' TO '2024-01-01T05:00:00.000000Z'
                FILL(LINEAR, NULL)
                """)
                .timestamp("ts")
                .noRandomAccess()
                .noLeakCheck()
                .returns("""
                        ts\tx\ty
                        2024-01-01T01:00:00.000000Z\t1.0\t10.0
                        2024-01-01T02:00:00.000000Z\t2.0\t20.0
                        2024-01-01T03:00:00.000000Z\tnull\tnull
                        2024-01-01T04:00:00.000000Z\tnull\tnull
                        """);
    });
}
```

On master it fails with: `java.lang.NullPointerException: Cannot invoke "io.questdb.cairo.sql.Record.getDouble(int)" because "rec" is null`

</details>

