body_text:
`CAST(c AS GEOHASH(1c))` turns a NULL CHAR into a NULL geohash, but inserting the same value into a GEOHASH(1c) column fails the whole statement.

### To reproduce

```sql
CREATE TABLE src (c CHAR);
INSERT INTO src VALUES ('u'), (NULL);
CREATE TABLE dst (g GEOHASH(1c));
INSERT INTO dst SELECT c FROM src;
```

Actual: `inconvertible value: \0 [CHAR -> GEOHASH(1c)]` (the message carries a raw NUL byte); nothing is inserted.
Expected: two rows, `u` and NULL.

Likely cause: `SqlUtil.implicitCastCharAsGeoHash` does not map CHAR 0 (NULL) to the geohash NULL.

Reproduced on master 6c63556431.

<details>
<summary>Failing test</summary>

Add to `core/src/test/java/io/questdb/test/griffin/InsertCastTest.java`:

```java
@Test
public void testCastCharNullGeoByteTab() throws Exception {
    assertMemoryLeak(() -> {
        execute("CREATE TABLE src (c CHAR)");
        execute("INSERT INTO src VALUES ('u'), (NULL)");
        execute("CREATE TABLE dst (g GEOHASH(1c))");
        // a NULL CHAR becomes a NULL geohash, as CAST(c AS GEOHASH(1c)) already gives
        execute("INSERT INTO dst SELECT c FROM src");
        assertQuery("SELECT g FROM dst")
                .noLeakCheck()
                .expectSize()
                .returns("""
                        g
                        u

                        """);
    });
}
```

On master it fails with: `ImplicitCastException: inconvertible value: \0 [CHAR -> GEOHASH(1c)]`

