body_text:
A QWP query that returns a DECIMAL with precision 9 or less fails, although PostgreSQL wire and HTTP read the same column. DECIMAL(10) and wider work.

### To reproduce

```sql
CREATE TABLE d (d5 DECIMAL(5,2), ts TIMESTAMP) TIMESTAMP(ts) PARTITION BY DAY WAL;
INSERT INTO d VALUES (123.45m, '2024-01-01');
```

Run `SELECT d5 FROM d` with the Java client's `QwpQueryClient`.

Actual: `status=6 QWP egress: unsupported column type DECIMAL(5,2)`.
Expected: `123.45`.

Likely cause: `QwpColumnTypeMapper.toWireType` has no case for DECIMAL8, DECIMAL16 and DECIMAL32.

Reproduced on master 6c63556431.

<details>
<summary>Failing test</summary>

Add to `core/src/test/java/io/questdb/test/cutlass/qwp/QwpEgressTypesExhaustiveTest.java`:

```java
@Test
public void testDecimal32() throws Exception {
    // DECIMAL(5,2) is stored in 4 bytes. QWP ingest writes such columns, so egress must read them.
    TestUtils.assertMemoryLeak(() -> {
        try (TestServerMain serverMain = startEgressServer()) {
            serverMain.execute("CREATE TABLE t(d DECIMAL(5,2), part_ts TIMESTAMP) "
                    + "TIMESTAMP(part_ts) PARTITION BY DAY WAL");
            serverMain.execute("INSERT INTO t VALUES (123.45m, 1::TIMESTAMP), (CAST(NULL AS DECIMAL(5,2)), 2::TIMESTAMP)");
            serverMain.awaitTable("t");

            final LongList rawValues = new LongList();
            final BoolList nulls = new BoolList();
            final int[] scale = {0};
            try (QwpQueryClient client = QwpQueryClient.fromConfig("ws::addr=127.0.0.1:" + HTTP_PORT + ";")) {
                client.connect();
                client.execute("SELECT d FROM t", new QwpColumnBatchHandler() {
                    @Override
                    public void onBatch(QwpColumnBatch batch) {
                        scale[0] = batch.getDecimalScale(0);
                        for (int r = 0; r < batch.getRowCount(); r++) {
                            boolean isNull = batch.isNull(0, r);
                            nulls.add(isNull);
                            rawValues.add(isNull ? 0L : batch.getLongValue(0, r));
                        }
                    }

                    @Override
                    public void onEnd(long totalRows) {
                    }

                    @Override
                    public void onError(byte status, String message) {
                        Assert.fail(message);
                    }
                });
            }
            Assert.assertEquals(2, scale[0]);
            // 123.45 with scale 2 -> unscaled 12_345
            Assert.assertEquals(12_345L, rawValues.getQuick(0));
            Assert.assertTrue(nulls.get(1));
        }
    });
}
```

On master it fails with: `java.lang.AssertionError: QWP egress: unsupported column type DECIMAL(5,2)`
</details>

