body_text:
QWP cannot write a LONG128 column, but the server reports this as a retryable write error rather than a schema mismatch, so the client resends the batch several times (8 to 11 seconds) before it gives up with "poisoned frame".

### To reproduce

```sql
CREATE TABLE l (v LONG128, ts TIMESTAMP) TIMESTAMP(ts) PARTITION BY DAY WAL;
```

Send one row with the Java client (`Sender.fromConfig("ws::addr=...")`): `table("l").uuidColumn("v", 7, 0).at(...)`.

Actual: `WRITE_ERROR: unsupported column type for columnar write: LONG128`, replayed 6 to 7 times.
Expected: an immediate `SCHEMA_MISMATCH` refusal, as for other columns QWP cannot write.

Likely cause: `QwpWalAppender` has no LONG128 case, and its fallback throws a plain `CairoException` instead of `CairoException.schemaMismatch()`.

Reproduced on master 6c63556431.

<details>
<summary>Failing test</summary>

Add to `core/src/test/java/io/questdb/test/cutlass/qwp/e2e/QwpWebSocketTypeConversionE2ETest.java`
(imports `io.questdb.client.LineSenderServerException`, `io.questdb.client.SenderError`,
`org.junit.Assert`, `java.util.concurrent.CompletableFuture`, `java.util.concurrent.TimeUnit`):

```java
@Test
public void testUuidToLong128ColumnIsSchemaMismatch() throws Exception {
    // QWP cannot write a LONG128 column. The server should refuse the batch as a schema mismatch,
    // like any other column it cannot write, so the client fails at once instead of replaying it.
    runInContext((port) -> {
        execute("CREATE TABLE tc_uuid_l128 (col LONG128, ts TIMESTAMP) TIMESTAMP(ts) PARTITION BY DAY WAL");

        final CompletableFuture<SenderError> firstErrFut = new CompletableFuture<>();
        final CompletableFuture<SenderError> terminalFut = new CompletableFuture<>();
        final QwpWebSocketSender sender = connectWs(port, err -> {
            if (err.getAppliedPolicy() == SenderError.Policy.TERMINAL) {
                terminalFut.complete(err);
            }
            firstErrFut.complete(err);
        }, 1);
        SenderError.Category expectedTerminalCategory = null;
        try {
            sender.table("tc_uuid_l128")
                    .uuidColumn("col", 1, 2)
                    .at(1_000_000_000_000L, ChronoUnit.MICROS);
            try {
                sender.flush();
            } catch (LineSenderServerException ignored) {
                // the I/O thread can latch the terminal before flush() polls for it
            }

            final SenderError err = firstErrFut.get(10, TimeUnit.SECONDS);
            Assert.assertEquals(err.getServerMessage(), SenderError.Category.SCHEMA_MISMATCH, err.getCategory());
            expectedTerminalCategory = SenderError.Category.SCHEMA_MISMATCH;
        } finally {
            assertRejectionTerminalOnClose(sender, terminalFut, expectedTerminalCategory);
        }
    });
}
```

On master it fails with: `java.lang.AssertionError: unsupported column type for columnar write: LONG128 expected:<SCHEMA_MISMATCH> but was:<WRITE_ERROR>`
</details>

