body_text:
If a conversion fails after `/exec` has started a 200 response, the server appends the headers of a second, 400 response. Clients cannot parse the result (`curl: (8) Header without colon`), so the user never sees the error.

### To reproduce

```sql
CREATE TABLE t (k VARCHAR, c CHAR);
INSERT INTO t VALUES ('digit', '1'), ('letter', 'a');
```

then `GET /exec?query=SELECT k, c::INT code FROM t`.

Actual:

```
HTTP/1.1 200 OK\r\n ... Keep-Alive: timeout=5, max=10000\r\n
HTTP/1.1 400 Bad request\r\n ... {"query":"SELECT k, c::INT code FROM t","error":"inconvertible value: a [CHAR -> INT]","position":0}
```

Expected: one well-formed response that carries the error, as for other errors after the header.

Likely cause: `JsonQueryProcessor` answers an `ImplicitCastException` with `sendException`, which starts a new response even after the 200 header went out.

Reproduced on master 6c63556431.

<details>
<summary>Failing test</summary>

Add to `core/src/test/java/io/questdb/test/cutlass/http/IODispatcherTest.java`:

```java
@Test
public void testQueryImplicitCastExceptionAfterFirstRecord() throws Exception {
    // The first row converts and the second does not. The 200 header is already out by then,
    // so the error must close the JSON the way any other error after the header does.
    getSimpleTester().run((engine, _) -> {
        try (SqlExecutionContext executionContext = TestUtils.createSqlExecutionCtx(engine)) {
            engine.execute("CREATE TABLE t (k VARCHAR, c CHAR)", executionContext);
            engine.execute("INSERT INTO t VALUES ('digit', '1'), ('letter', 'a')", executionContext);

            testHttpClient.assertGet(
                    "/exec",
                    "{\"query\":\"SELECT k, c::INT code FROM t\",\"columns\":[{\"name\":\"k\",\"type\":\"VARCHAR\"},{\"name\":\"code\",\"type\":\"INT\"}],"
                            + "\"timestamp\":-1,\"dataset\":[[\"digit\",1],[]],\"count\":2,"
                            + "\"error\":\"inconvertible value: a [CHAR -> INT]\", \"errorPos\":0}",
                    "SELECT k, c::INT code FROM t"
            );
        }
    });
}
```

On master it fails with: `io.questdb.cutlass.http.client.HttpClientException: malformed chunk size`

</details>

