body_text:
### Describe the bug

When an out-of-order commit rewrites partitions that have a POSTING index, and the server is killed after the
index of a partition was resealed but before the commit reached `_txn`, the next start leaves superseded index
generations (`<column>.pv.<n>` and `<column>.pc<i>.<v>.<n>` files) in that partition. Later commits and the purge
jobs never remove them. Queries still return correct rows; the cost is disk space, one or two extra index
generations per partition and POSTING column for each such crash.

A kill after the `_txn` commit but before the posting purge job ran leaks the superseded generation the same way.

### To reproduce

1. Create a WAL table with POSTING indexes and fill three days:
   ```sql
   CREATE TABLE t (ts TIMESTAMP, s SYMBOL INDEX TYPE POSTING INCLUDE (v), k SYMBOL INDEX TYPE POSTING, v LONG)
       TIMESTAMP(ts) PARTITION BY DAY WAL DEDUP UPSERT KEYS(ts, s);
   ```
   Insert rows into 2024-01-01, 2024-01-02 and 2024-01-03 and let the WAL apply them.
2. Insert one more batch with rows in all three days, so that the WAL apply runs one out-of-order commit over all
   three partitions.
3. Kill the server while that commit runs, after a partition's index was resealed and before `_txn` was written.
4. Start the server, let the WAL apply replay the commit, insert one more batch into the same three days and let the
   purge jobs run.
5. List a partition directory, for example `t~1/2024-01-01/`: it holds two or three `.pv` files per POSTING column
   instead of one.

The window in step 3 is short, so the test below models the kill: it copies the table directory at about 80
evenly spaced file operations of the commit (a kill keeps every byte already written), restarts on each copy and
checks that each partition has exactly one index generation per POSTING column. Kill point 0 is a control: the copy
is taken after the commit and the purge job have finished, and it passes. Put the test in
`core/src/test/java/io/questdb/test/cairo/` and run from the repository root (about 6 minutes for both modes):

```
mvn -pl core test -Dtest.include="%regex[.*PostingIndexKillMidO3Test.*]" -Dtest="**/PostingIndexKillMidO3Test.java" -DfailIfNoTests=false -Dsurefire.failIfNoSpecifiedTests=false
```

<details><summary>Reproducer test</summary>

```java
package io.questdb.test.cairo;

import io.questdb.PropertyKey;
import io.questdb.cairo.CairoEngine;
import io.questdb.cairo.O3PartitionPurgeJob;
import io.questdb.cairo.PostingSealPurgeJob;
import io.questdb.cairo.TableToken;
import io.questdb.std.FilesFacade;
import io.questdb.std.Os;
import io.questdb.std.str.LPSZ;
import io.questdb.std.str.StringSink;
import io.questdb.test.AbstractCairoTest;
import io.questdb.test.std.TestFilesFacadeImpl;
import io.questdb.test.tools.TestUtils;
import org.junit.Assert;
import org.junit.Test;
import org.junit.runner.RunWith;
import org.junit.runners.Parameterized;

import java.io.IOException;
import java.io.UncheckedIOException;
import java.nio.file.Files;
import java.nio.file.Path;
import java.nio.file.Paths;
import java.nio.file.StandardCopyOption;
import java.util.ArrayList;
import java.util.Collection;
import java.util.Comparator;
import java.util.List;
import java.util.Map;
import java.util.TreeMap;
import java.util.regex.Pattern;
import java.util.stream.Stream;

/**
 * A process kill during an out-of-order commit that rewrites the POSTING index of older partitions. A kill keeps
 * every byte already written, so the test models it as a copy of the table directory taken at a file operation of
 * the commit. For about 80 evenly spaced operations of one such commit it restarts from the copy, replays the WAL,
 * makes one more out-of-order commit into the same partitions, runs the purge jobs and checks that the rows read
 * correctly through the index and that each partition holds exactly one index generation per POSTING column.
 * Kill point 0 is the control: the copy is taken after the commit and the purge job.
 */
@RunWith(Parameterized.class)
public class PostingIndexKillMidO3Test extends AbstractCairoTest {
    private static final long DAY = 86_400_000_000L;
    private static final long DAY1 = 1_704_067_200_000_000L; // 2024-01-01T00:00:00Z
    private static final long HOUR = 3_600_000_000L;
    private static final int ROWS_PER_PASS = 10;
    private static final Pattern SEALED_FILE = Pattern.compile("[sk]\\.(pv|pc\\d+)\\..*");
    private static final int KILL_POINTS = 80;
    private static final int SYMBOLS = 4;
    private static volatile long killAtOp = -1;
    private static String killedAt;
    private static long ops;
    private static Path snapshot;
    private static Path snapshotSource;
    private static final FilesFacade KILL_FF = new TestFilesFacadeImpl() {
        @Override
        public boolean allocate(long fd, long size) {
            tick("allocate", null);
            return super.allocate(fd, size);
        }

        @Override
        public boolean close(long fd) {
            tick("close", null);
            return super.close(fd);
        }

        @Override
        public long openRW(LPSZ name, int opts) {
            tick("openRW", name);
            return super.openRW(name, opts);
        }

        @Override
        public void remove(LPSZ name) {
            tick("remove", name);
            super.remove(name);
        }

        @Override
        public boolean removeQuiet(LPSZ name) {
            tick("removeQuiet", name);
            return super.removeQuiet(name);
        }

        @Override
        public int rename(LPSZ from, LPSZ to) {
            tick("rename", from);
            return super.rename(from, to);
        }

        @Override
        public boolean truncate(long fd, long size) {
            tick("truncate", null);
            return super.truncate(fd, size);
        }
    };
    private final String mode;

    public PostingIndexKillMidO3Test(String mode) {
        this.mode = mode;
    }

    @Parameterized.Parameters(name = "{0}")
    public static Collection<Object[]> data() {
        return List.of(new Object[]{"nosync"}, new Object[]{"sync"});
    }

    @Test
    public void testKillDuringO3CommitIntoOlderPartitions() throws Exception {
        setProperty(PropertyKey.CAIRO_COMMIT_MODE, mode);
        setProperty(PropertyKey.CAIRO_SQL_COLUMN_PURGE_RETRY_DELAY, 1);
        setProperty(PropertyKey.CAIRO_SQL_COLUMN_PURGE_RETRY_DELAY_LIMIT, 1);
        assertMemoryLeak(KILL_FF, () -> {
            final StringBuilder failures = new StringBuilder();
            int swept = 0;
            int beforeCommit = 0;
            int afterCommit = 0;
            // Count the file operations of one such commit, then kill at about KILL_POINTS of them, evenly spaced.
            final long commitOps = countCommitOps();
            final long stride = Math.max(1, commitOps / KILL_POINTS);
            for (long op = 0; op <= commitOps; op = op == 0 ? 1 : op + stride) {
                final String table = "k" + op;
                execute("CREATE TABLE " + table + " (ts TIMESTAMP, s SYMBOL INDEX TYPE POSTING INCLUDE (v), k SYMBOL INDEX TYPE POSTING, "
                        + "v LONG) TIMESTAMP(ts) PARTITION BY DAY WAL DEDUP UPSERT KEYS(ts, s)");
                execute(threeDaySql(table, 0));
                drainWalQueue();
                runPurgeJobs(engine);
                final TableToken token = engine.verifyTableName(table);
                final Path tableDir = Paths.get(root, token.getDirName());
                snapshotSource = tableDir;
                snapshot = Paths.get(root).getParent().resolve("kill-snapshot-" + mode + "-" + op);

                // Pass 1 writes into all three days: one out-of-order commit that rewrites all three partitions.
                execute(threeDaySql(table, 1));
                ops = 0;
                killAtOp = op;
                try {
                    drainWalQueue();
                } finally {
                    killAtOp = -1;
                }
                if (op == 0) {
                    // the control: the commit and its purges complete, then a restart
                    runPurgeJobs(engine);
                    copyDir(tableDir, snapshot);
                    killedAt = "after the commit and the purge job";
                } else if (!Files.exists(snapshot)) {
                    // past the last file operation of the commit
                    break;
                }
                swept++;
                engine.releaseAllReaders();
                engine.releaseAllWriters();
                engine.releaseInactive();

                // The restart: the table directory as the kill left it, a new engine.
                deleteDir(tableDir);
                copyDir(snapshot, tableDir);
                deleteDir(snapshot);
                try (CairoEngine restarted = new CairoEngine(configuration)) {
                    final StringSink sink = new StringSink();
                    restarted.print("SELECT count() FROM " + table, sink);
                    final boolean committed = sink.toString().equals("count\n" + 2 * ROWS_PER_PASS + "\n");
                    final String where = "kill at op " + op + " (" + killedAt + ", " + (committed ? "after" : "before") + " the _txn commit)";
                    TestUtils.drainWalQueue(restarted);
                    restarted.execute(threeDaySql(table, 2));
                    TestUtils.drainWalQueue(restarted);
                    runPurgeJobs(restarted);
                    try {
                        assertRowsThroughIndex(restarted, table, where);
                        assertOneGenerationPerPartitionAndColumn(tableDir, where);
                    } catch (AssertionError e) {
                        if (op == 0) {
                            throw new AssertionError("the control (no kill) fails, the check is wrong: " + e.getMessage(), e);
                        }
                        failures.append(e.getMessage()).append('\n');
                        if (committed) {
                            afterCommit++;
                        } else {
                            beforeCommit++;
                        }
                    }
                }
            }
            System.out.println("REPRO mode=" + mode + " file operations in the commit=" + commitOps + ", kill points swept=" + swept + ", failing before the _txn commit=" + beforeCommit
                    + ", failing after it=" + afterCommit + "\n" + failures);
            Assert.assertTrue("kill points swept: " + swept, swept > 3);
            Assert.assertEquals("", failures.toString());
        });
    }

    private static void assertOneGenerationPerPartitionAndColumn(Path tableDir, String where) {
        final Map<String, List<String>> byPartitionAndColumn = new TreeMap<>();
        try (Stream<Path> paths = Files.walk(tableDir)) {
            paths.filter(p -> SEALED_FILE.matcher(p.getFileName().toString()).matches()).sorted().forEach(p -> {
                final String name = p.getFileName().toString();
                final String key = p.getParent().getFileName() + "/" + name.substring(0, name.indexOf('.'));
                byPartitionAndColumn.computeIfAbsent(key, k -> new ArrayList<>()).add(name);
            });
        } catch (IOException e) {
            throw new UncheckedIOException(e);
        }
        Assert.assertEquals(where + ": partitions and columns with index files " + byPartitionAndColumn.keySet(), 6, byPartitionAndColumn.size());
        final StringBuilder extra = new StringBuilder();
        for (Map.Entry<String, List<String>> e : byPartitionAndColumn.entrySet()) {
            String sealTxn = null;
            int generations = 0;
            for (String name : e.getValue()) {
                if (name.contains(".pv.")) {
                    generations++;
                    sealTxn = name.substring(name.lastIndexOf('.'));
                }
            }
            boolean coversMatch = true;
            for (String name : e.getValue()) {
                coversMatch &= sealTxn != null && name.endsWith(sealTxn);
            }
            if (generations != 1 || !coversMatch) {
                extra.append(extra.isEmpty() ? "" : "; ").append(e.getKey()).append(' ').append(e.getValue());
            }
        }
        Assert.assertTrue(where + ": more than one index generation in " + extra, extra.isEmpty());
    }

    private static void assertRowsThroughIndex(CairoEngine e, String table, String where) throws Exception {
        final long[] count = new long[SYMBOLS + 3];
        final long[] sum = new long[SYMBOLS + 3];
        for (int pass = 0; pass <= 2; pass++) {
            for (int i = 0; i < ROWS_PER_PASS; i++) {
                final long v = (long) pass * ROWS_PER_PASS + i;
                count[(int) (v % SYMBOLS)]++;
                sum[(int) (v % SYMBOLS)] += v;
                count[SYMBOLS + (int) (v % 3)]++;
                sum[SYMBOLS + (int) (v % 3)] += v;
            }
        }
        final StringSink sink = new StringSink();
        for (int k = 0; k < SYMBOLS + 3; k++) {
            final String filter = k < SYMBOLS ? "s = '" + (char) ('a' + k) + "'" : "k = '" + (char) ('p' + k - SYMBOLS) + "'";
            e.print("SELECT count(), sum(v) FROM " + table + " WHERE " + filter, sink);
            Assert.assertEquals(where + ": " + filter, "count\tsum\n" + count[k] + "\t" + sum[k] + "\n", sink.toString());
        }
    }

    private static long countCommitOps() throws Exception {
        execute("CREATE TABLE calibrate (ts TIMESTAMP, s SYMBOL INDEX TYPE POSTING INCLUDE (v), k SYMBOL INDEX TYPE POSTING, "
                + "v LONG) TIMESTAMP(ts) PARTITION BY DAY WAL DEDUP UPSERT KEYS(ts, s)");
        execute(threeDaySql("calibrate", 0));
        drainWalQueue();
        runPurgeJobs(engine);
        execute(threeDaySql("calibrate", 1));
        ops = 0;
        killAtOp = Long.MAX_VALUE;
        try {
            drainWalQueue();
        } finally {
            killAtOp = -1;
        }
        return ops;
    }

    private static void copyDir(Path from, Path to) {
        try (Stream<Path> paths = Files.walk(from)) {
            for (Path p : (Iterable<Path>) paths::iterator) {
                final Path target = to.resolve(from.relativize(p).toString());
                if (Files.isDirectory(p)) {
                    Files.createDirectories(target);
                } else {
                    Files.copy(p, target, StandardCopyOption.REPLACE_EXISTING);
                }
            }
        } catch (IOException e) {
            throw new UncheckedIOException(e);
        }
    }

    private static void deleteDir(Path dir) {
        try (Stream<Path> paths = Files.walk(dir)) {
            for (Path p : (Iterable<Path>) paths.sorted(Comparator.reverseOrder())::iterator) {
                Files.delete(p);
            }
        } catch (IOException e) {
            throw new UncheckedIOException(e);
        }
    }

    private static void runPurgeJobs(CairoEngine e) throws Exception {
        try (
                PostingSealPurgeJob job = new PostingSealPurgeJob(e);
                O3PartitionPurgeJob partitionPurge = new O3PartitionPurgeJob(e, 1)
        ) {
            for (int i = 0; i < 4; i++) {
                Os.sleep(1);
                job.run();
            }
            //noinspection StatementWithEmptyBody
            while (partitionPurge.run()) {
            }
        }
    }

    private static String threeDaySql(String table, int pass) {
        final StringBuilder sql = new StringBuilder("INSERT INTO ").append(table).append(" VALUES ");
        for (int i = 0; i < ROWS_PER_PASS; i++) {
            final long v = (long) pass * ROWS_PER_PASS + i;
            final long ts = DAY1 + (i % 3) * DAY + 10L * HOUR + pass * 600_000_000L + i * 30_000_000L;
            sql.append(i == 0 ? "" : ", ").append('(').append(ts).append("::timestamp, '")
                    .append((char) ('a' + v % SYMBOLS)).append("', '").append((char) ('p' + v % 3)).append("', ")
                    .append(v).append(')');
        }
        return sql.toString();
    }

    private static void tick(String what, LPSZ name) {
        if (killAtOp > 0 && ++ops == killAtOp) {
            copyDir(snapshotSource, snapshot);
            killedAt = name != null ? what + " " + Paths.get(name.asAsciiCharSequence().toString()).getFileName() : what;
        }
    }
}
```

</details>

### Expected behaviour

After the restart, the replay and the next commit, each partition keeps one index generation per POSTING column,
as it does without a crash (the control case).

### Actual behaviour

