Put the file under `core/src/test/java/io/questdb/test/cairo/` and run, from the repository root:

```
mvn -B test -pl core -Dtest.include="%regex[.*SyncAlterColumnTypeSymbolDurabilityTest.*]" -DfailIfNoTests=false -Dsurefire.failIfNoSpecifiedTests=false
```

### Expected behaviour

In SYNC mode, by the time the `ALTER` returns, the symbol map, the key column files, the index files and their
directory entries are on disk, flushed before `_txn` and `_meta` name them. After a power loss the table reads back
the converted values, through the index too.

### Actual behaviour

All three tests (to SYMBOL non-WAL and WAL, to SYMBOL INDEX non-WAL) fail. To SYMBOL INDEX:

```
java.lang.AssertionError: after a power loss the table does not read back; files never flushed:
[x~/2024-01-01/v.d.1 (name and content not flushed), x~/2024-01-01/v.k.1 (name and content not flushed),
x~/2024-01-01/v.v.1 (name and content not flushed), x~/2024-01-02/v.d.1 (name and content not flushed),
x~/2024-01-02/v.k.1 (name and content not flushed), x~/2024-01-02/v.v.1 (name and content not flushed),
x~/2024-01-03/v.d.1 (name not flushed), x~/2024-01-03/v.k.1 (name and content not flushed),
x~/2024-01-03/v.v.1 (name and content not flushed), x~/v.c.1 (name and content not flushed),
x~/v.k.1 (name not flushed), x~/v.o.1 (name not flushed), x~/v.v.1 (name and content not flushed)];
error: [18] [2]: SymbolMap does not exist: <dbRoot>/x~/v.o.1
```

An `strace` of the same run, matching each `msync` to its mapping, shows exactly the same set of files never
flushed, at the system call level.

### Verified on

Master `77c6cf2d6b`, 9 October 2026, Linux 7.1 x86_64, ext4. ALTER COLUMN TYPE was added in 8.0.0, so every release
since then is likely affected (not run on a release build).

### Suggested fix

When the commit mode is not NOSYNC, before `_txn` and `_meta` are committed:

- in `TableWriter.changeColumnType`, after `convertOperator.convertColumn(...)` for a SYMBOL target, call
  `sync(false)` on the new column's `SymbolMapWriter` and `fsync` the table directory;
- flush the converted key column files and their partition directories in `ConvertOperatorImpl` (the same fix as the
  ALTER COLUMN TYPE values issue);
- after `TableWriter.writeIndex`, flush each partition's new index files and then that partition's directory. This is
  the same fix as for ALTER COLUMN ... ADD INDEX, which goes through `writeIndex` too.

Not tried.

### Additional context

Found while working on questdb#7411 (adaptive commit mode). Related: #1857 (SYNC mode does not `msync` all written
data). The values of a plain ALTER COLUMN TYPE and ALTER COLUMN ... ADD INDEX have the same kind of gap, reported
separately.
