body_text:
## Problem

An O3 commit that updates a parquet partition in place keeps the partition directory and its name txn. `O3PartitionJob.updateParquetIndexes` then rebuilds the index of every indexed SYMBOL column inside that live directory, under the same file names, for the merged row layout. A query that opened its cursor before the commit still decodes the previous parquet footer, but its index reader picks up the rebuilt files, so the cursor reads old-layout rows at new-layout row ids.

The query returns rows that don't match its filter and misses rows that do. Queries that start after the commit return correct results.

## Impact

- Index-driven queries on an indexed SYMBOL column (for example `WHERE s = 'a'` with an `Index forward scan` plan) return wrong rows when an in-place O3 commit lands on a parquet partition they read. BITMAP, the default index type, is affected.
- The O3 merge takes the in-place path when the parquet partition has more than one row group, its unused bytes stay under `cairo.partition.encoder.parquet.o3.rewrite.unused.ratio` (0.5) and `cairo.partition.encoder.parquet.o3.rewrite.unused.max.bytes` (1 GiB), and nothing else forces a rewrite, for example a schema change or a dedup boundary tie. With the default row group size of 100,000 rows, a partition needs more than 100,000 rows to have several row groups.
- A rewrite builds the index in a new txn directory and leaves the live files alone, so rewrites are not affected.
- Not checked: POSTING indexes, and whether a reader that touches a mapped index page past the truncated end of file during the rebuild can fault rather than return wrong rows.

## Location

On master `c22be38bb`, in `core/src/main/java/io/questdb/cairo/`:

- `O3PartitionJob.processParquetPartition` passes the live directory's name txn (`srcNameTxn`) to `updateParquetIndexes` in update mode ([O3PartitionJob.java L594-L616](https://github.com/questdb/questdb/blob/c22be38bbab4909236ddfb00179d76cfe11d632d/core/src/main/java/io/questdb/cairo/O3PartitionJob.java#L594-L616)).
- `updateParquetIndexes` opens each index writer in that directory with a positive block capacity ([O3PartitionJob.java L3580-L3634](https://github.com/questdb/questdb/blob/c22be38bbab4909236ddfb00179d76cfe11d632d/core/src/main/java/io/questdb/cairo/O3PartitionJob.java#L3580-L3634)).
- With a positive capacity, `BitmapIndexWriter.of(Path, CharSequence, long, int)` truncates the `.k` file through `initKeyMemory` and truncates the `.v` file ([BitmapIndexWriter.java L291-L346](https://github.com/questdb/questdb/blob/c22be38bbab4909236ddfb00179d76cfe11d632d/core/src/main/java/io/questdb/cairo/idx/BitmapIndexWriter.java#L291-L346), [L74-L80](https://github.com/questdb/questdb/blob/c22be38bbab4909236ddfb00179d76cfe11d632d/core/src/main/java/io/questdb/cairo/idx/BitmapIndexWriter.java#L74-L80)).
- The index file names depend only on the column name txn and the partition name txn, and an in-place update changes neither. A reader pinned to the previous txn therefore opens or reloads the rebuilt files. For example, `TableReader.getIndexReader` reuses a cached index reader and calls `reloadConditionally()` when both txns are unchanged ([TableReader.java L375-L427](https://github.com/questdb/questdb/blob/c22be38bbab4909236ddfb00179d76cfe11d632d/core/src/main/java/io/questdb/cairo/TableReader.java#L375-L427)).

## Reproduction

The test below fails on master `c22be38bb`. Its row group size and rewrite thresholds only keep the 13-row partition on the in-place path, and it asserts that the partition name txn does not change.

```java
package io.questdb.test.cairo.parquet;

import io.questdb.PropertyKey;
import io.questdb.cairo.TableReader;
import io.questdb.cairo.sql.RecordCursor;
import io.questdb.cairo.sql.RecordCursorFactory;
import io.questdb.std.str.StringSink;
import io.questdb.test.AbstractCairoTest;
import io.questdb.test.tools.TestUtils;
import org.junit.Assert;
import org.junit.Test;

public class ParquetInPlaceIndexStaleCursorReproTest extends AbstractCairoTest {

    @Test
    public void testCursorOpenedBeforeInPlaceO3KeepsItsSnapshot() throws Exception {
        // small row groups and permissive rewrite thresholds keep the O3 merge in place
        node1.setProperty(PropertyKey.CAIRO_PARTITION_ENCODER_PARQUET_ROW_GROUP_SIZE, 4);
        node1.setProperty(PropertyKey.CAIRO_PARTITION_ENCODER_PARQUET_O3_REWRITE_UNUSED_RATIO, "1.0");
        node1.setProperty(PropertyKey.CAIRO_PARTITION_ENCODER_PARQUET_O3_REWRITE_UNUSED_MAX_BYTES, Long.MAX_VALUE);
        assertMemoryLeak(() -> {
            execute("CREATE TABLE pt (s SYMBOL INDEX, v INT, ts TIMESTAMP) TIMESTAMP(ts) PARTITION BY DAY WAL");
            execute("""
                    INSERT INTO pt VALUES
                    ('a', 1, '2024-01-01T00:00:00.000000Z'), ('b', 2, '2024-01-01T01:00:00.000000Z'),
                    ('c', 3, '2024-01-01T02:00:00.000000Z'), ('a', 4, '2024-01-01T03:00:00.000000Z'),
                    ('b', 5, '2024-01-01T04:00:00.000000Z'), ('c', 6, '2024-01-01T05:00:00.000000Z'),
                    ('a', 7, '2024-01-01T06:00:00.000000Z'), ('b', 8, '2024-01-01T07:00:00.000000Z'),
                    ('c', 9, '2024-01-01T08:00:00.000000Z'), ('a', 10, '2024-01-01T09:00:00.000000Z'),
                    ('b', 11, '2024-01-01T10:00:00.000000Z'), ('c', 12, '2024-01-01T11:00:00.000000Z'),
                    ('a', 99, '2024-01-02T00:00:00.000000Z')""");
            drainWalQueue();
            execute("ALTER TABLE pt CONVERT PARTITION TO PARQUET LIST '2024-01-01'");
            drainWalQueue();

            final long nameTxn = getPartitionNameTxn();
            try (
                    RecordCursorFactory factory = select("SELECT s, v, ts FROM pt WHERE s = 'a' AND ts IN '2024-01-01'");
                    RecordCursor cursor = factory.getCursor(sqlExecutionContext)
            ) {
                // O3 commit into the parquet partition while the cursor is open
                execute("INSERT INTO pt VALUES ('a', 101, '2024-01-01T04:30:00.000000Z')");
                drainWalQueue();
                Assert.assertEquals("O3 merge must update the parquet partition in place", nameTxn, getPartitionNameTxn());

                // the cursor was opened before the commit, so it must return the pre-commit 'a' rows
                TestUtils.assertCursor(
                        """
                                s\tv\tts
                                a\t1\t2024-01-01T00:00:00.000000Z
                                a\t4\t2024-01-01T03:00:00.000000Z
                                a\t7\t2024-01-01T06:00:00.000000Z
                                a\t10\t2024-01-01T09:00:00.000000Z
                                """,
                        cursor,
                        factory.getMetadata(),
                        true,
                        new StringSink()
                );
            }
        });
    }

    private static long getPartitionNameTxn() {
        try (TableReader reader = getReader("pt")) {
            Assert.assertTrue(reader.getTxFile().isPartitionParquet(0));
            return reader.getTxFile().getPartitionNameTxn(0);
        }
    }
}
```

Output:

```
expected:<s	v	ts
a	1	2024-01-01T00:00:00.000000Z
a	4	2024-01-01T03:00:00.000000Z
a	7	2024-01-01T06:00:00.000000Z
a	10	2024-01-01T09:00:00.000000Z
> but was:<s	v	ts
a	1	2024-01-01T00:00:00.000000Z
a	4	2024-01-01T03:00:00.000000Z
c	6	2024-01-01T05:00:00.000000Z
b	8	2024-01-01T07:00:00.000000Z
b	11	2024-01-01T10:00:00.000000Z
>
```

## Suggested fix

Version the index files that an in-place update rebuilds, for example under a new column name txn committed with the update, and purge the old files through the scoreboard-gated purge path once no reader uses them. `deferParquetPostingSealPurges` already defers posting `.pv` purges this way.

Found while reviewing #7880. The bug exists on master for every parquet partition that takes the in-place path. #7880 adds tables with a type-converted column to that group: master rewrites their parquet partitions on every O3 commit after `ALTER COLUMN TYPE`, while with #7880 the first commit rewrites the file and later commits can update it in place.

