body_text:
If opening or mapping a column file fails while a WAL commit with out-of-order rows is applied, and
the table has a dropped column, the apply job never finishes: it waits forever for column work that
is already over. The table stops applying transactions but is not suspended, so `RESUME WAL` does not
help, and the worker thread stays busy until restart. Without a dropped column the same failure
suspends the table cleanly, as expected.

### To reproduce

The trigger is an operating-system file failure (out of file descriptors, `vm.max_map_count`
reached, disk full, I/O error) during the commit, so plain SQL cannot cause it on demand. The shape:

```sql
CREATE TABLE x (a INT, b INT, c INT, ts TIMESTAMP) TIMESTAMP(ts) PARTITION BY DAY WAL;
INSERT INTO x VALUES
    (1, 1, 1, '1970-01-01T00:00:00.000000Z'),
    (2, 2, 2, '1970-01-01T02:00:00.000000Z'),
    (3, 3, 3, '1970-01-02T00:00:00.000000Z');
ALTER TABLE x DROP COLUMN c;
-- this row lands inside partition 1970-01-01; opening a.d of that partition fails
INSERT INTO x VALUES (4, 4, '1970-01-01T01:00:00.000000Z');
```

Actual: the WAL apply job spins in `TableWriter.o3ConsumePartitionUpdates()` forever; the table is never suspended.
Expected: the table is suspended with the file error, and `ALTER TABLE x RESUME WAL` applies the row once the cause is gone.

The same hang happens when out-of-order rows are appended to the last partition (all newer than the
table's max timestamp, out of order within the commit) and mapping a column file fails; there any
dropped column is enough.

Likely cause: the column counter that tells the writer when all column work of a partition is done
counts only live columns, but the error paths subtract a count that includes dropped columns. In
`O3PartitionJob.publishOpenColumnTasks()` the error path subtracts every column after the failing one,
dropped ones included; in the last-partition append loop of `TableWriter` it subtracts against the
total column count. The counter steps past zero, nobody sees it reach zero, and the partition is
never reported done.

Reproduced on master e4da5b4543.

<details>
<summary>Failing test</summary>

Add to `core/src/test/java/io/questdb/test/cairo/o3/O3FailureTest.java` (needs `import io.questdb.cairo.TableToken;`):

```java
    @Test(timeout = 120_000)
    public void testWalMidMergeOpenRwFailBeforeDroppedColumnContended() throws Exception {
        // WAL apply runs an O3 merge into a mid partition and fails to open column 'a', which
        // sits before the dropped column 'c'. The apply must suspend the table, not wait forever.
        final AtomicBoolean isArmed = new AtomicBoolean(false);
        executeWithPool(
                0,
                (engine, compiler, sqlExecutionContext, timestampTypeName) -> {
                    engine.execute(
                            "CREATE TABLE x (a INT, b INT, c INT, ts " + timestampTypeName + ") TIMESTAMP(ts) PARTITION BY DAY WAL",
                            sqlExecutionContext
                    );
                    engine.execute(
                            """
                                    INSERT INTO x VALUES
                                    (1, 1, 1, '1970-01-01T00:00:00.000000Z'),
                                    (2, 2, 2, '1970-01-01T02:00:00.000000Z'),
                                    (3, 3, 3, '1970-01-02T00:00:00.000000Z')
                                    """,
                            sqlExecutionContext
                    );
                    engine.execute("ALTER TABLE x DROP COLUMN c", sqlExecutionContext);
                    drainWalQueue(engine);
                    final TableToken tableToken = engine.verifyTableName("x");
                    Assert.assertFalse(engine.getTableSequencerAPI().isSuspended(tableToken));

                    isArmed.set(true);
                    engine.execute("INSERT INTO x VALUES (4, 4, '1970-01-01T01:00:00.000000Z')", sqlExecutionContext);
                    drainWalQueue(engine);
                    Assert.assertTrue(engine.getTableSequencerAPI().isSuspended(tableToken));

                    isArmed.set(false);
                    engine.execute("ALTER TABLE x RESUME WAL", sqlExecutionContext);
                    drainWalQueue(engine);
                    Assert.assertFalse(engine.getTableSequencerAPI().isSuspended(tableToken));
                    TestUtils.printSql(compiler, sqlExecutionContext, "SELECT a, b FROM x", sink2);
                    TestUtils.assertEquals(
                            """
                                    a\tb
                                    1\t1
                                    4\t4
                                    2\t2
                                    3\t3
                                    """,
                            sink2
                    );
                },
                new TestFilesFacadeImpl() {
                    @Override
                    public long openRW(LPSZ name, int opts) {
                        if (isArmed.get() && Utf8s.containsAscii(name, "1970-01-01.") && Utf8s.endsWithAscii(name, Files.SEPARATOR + "a.d")) {
                            return -1;
                        }
                        return super.openRW(name, opts);
                    }
                }
        );
    }
```

On master it fails with: `org.junit.runners.model.TestTimedOutException: test timed out after 120000 milliseconds`
at `TableWriter.o3ConsumePartitionUpdates(TableWriter.java:9547)`.

</details>

