body_text:
A set operation over two geohash columns keeps the coarser precision. When the two precisions are close
(for example GEOHASH(2c) and GEOHASH(3c), or GEOHASH(3b) and GEOHASH(5b)), the finer value is cut to its
trailing characters instead of its leading ones, so UNION ALL prints a different cell and UNION, INTERSECT
and EXCEPT match the wrong rows. Pairs whose precisions are further apart (GEOHASH(2c) and GEOHASH(5c)) work.

### To reproduce

```sql
CREATE TABLE a (g GEOHASH(2c));
INSERT INTO a VALUES ('sp');
CREATE TABLE b (g GEOHASH(3c));
INSERT INTO b VALUES ('spz');

SELECT g FROM a UNION ALL SELECT g FROM b;
SELECT g FROM a INTERSECT SELECT g FROM b;
```

Actual: UNION ALL returns `sp`, `pz`; INTERSECT returns no rows (EXCEPT returns `sp`, UNION returns both).
Expected: UNION ALL returns `sp`, `sp`; INTERSECT returns `sp`, the cell that contains `spz`.

It happens whenever both precisions fit the same storage size: 1-7 bits, 8-15 bits, 16-31 bits or
32-60 bits.

Likely cause: `SqlCodeGenerator.generateCastFunctions()` returns the column as is when both geohash types
have the same storage size, instead of cutting the finer one with `CastGeoHashToGeoHashFunctionFactory`,
as it does when the storage sizes differ.

Reproduced on master e4da5b4543.

<details>
<summary>Failing test</summary>

Add to `core/src/test/java/io/questdb/test/griffin/UnionAllCastTest.java`:

```java
    @Test
    public void testGeoSameStorageNarrowsToPrefix() throws Exception {
        // Each pair shares a storage width (GEOBYTE, GEOSHORT, GEOINT, GEOLONG) and differs in
        // precision. The set operation keeps the coarser precision, so the wider value must be
        // cut to its leading bits, the cell that contains it.
        assertMemoryLeak(() -> {
            final String[][] pairs = {
                    {"3b", "5b", "##101", "##10111", "101"},
                    {"2c", "3c", "'sp'", "'spz'", "sp"},
                    {"4c", "6c", "'sp01'", "'sp01zz'", "sp01"},
                    {"7c", "12c", "'sp01zzz'", "'sp01zzz12345'", "sp01zzz"},
            };
            for (int i = 0; i < pairs.length; i++) {
                final String[] pair = pairs[i];
                final String narrow = "narrow" + i;
                final String wide = "wide" + i;
                execute("CREATE TABLE " + narrow + " (g GEOHASH(" + pair[0] + "))");
                execute("INSERT INTO " + narrow + " VALUES (" + pair[2] + ")");
                execute("CREATE TABLE " + wide + " (g GEOHASH(" + pair[1] + "))");
                execute("INSERT INTO " + wide + " VALUES (" + pair[3] + ")");
                final String prefix = pair[4];

                assertQuery("SELECT g FROM " + narrow + " UNION ALL SELECT g FROM " + wide)
                        .noRandomAccess()
                        .expectSize()
                        .returns("g\n" + prefix + "\n" + prefix + "\n");
                assertQuery("SELECT g FROM " + wide + " UNION ALL SELECT g FROM " + narrow)
                        .noRandomAccess()
                        .expectSize()
                        .returns("g\n" + prefix + "\n" + prefix + "\n");
                assertQuery("SELECT g FROM " + narrow + " UNION SELECT g FROM " + wide)
                        .noRandomAccess()
                        .returns("g\n" + prefix + "\n");
                assertQuery("SELECT g FROM " + narrow + " INTERSECT SELECT g FROM " + wide)
                        .returns("g\n" + prefix + "\n");
                assertQuery("SELECT g FROM " + narrow + " EXCEPT SELECT g FROM " + wide)
                        .returns("g\n");
            }
        });
    }
