body_text:
Several string functions fail with an `UnsupportedOperationException` (no message) when they get an
IPv4 column, and `length_bytes()` fails the same way on a SYMBOL column. `arg_max()` over an IPv4
column fails with "unexpected reduce error". The same calls work when the argument is cast to
VARCHAR explicitly.

### To reproduce

```sql
CREATE TABLE t (ip IPv4, s SYMBOL, v VARCHAR, d DOUBLE);
INSERT INTO t VALUES ('1.2.3.4', 'abc', '1.2', 1.0), ('10.0.0.1', 'тест', '10', 2.0);

SELECT length_bytes(ip) FROM t;
SELECT starts_with(ip, v) FROM t;
SELECT strpos(ip, v) FROM t;
SELECT nullif(v, ip) FROM t;
SELECT replace(ip, v, v) FROM t;
SELECT json_extract(ip, '$.a') FROM t;
SELECT arg_max(ip, d) FROM t;
SELECT length_bytes(s) FROM t;
```

Actual: each query fails with `java.lang.UnsupportedOperationException` (an empty error message),
`arg_max` with `unexpected reduce error`.
Expected: the same result as with `ip::VARCHAR` / `s::VARCHAR`, e.g. `7` and `8` for
`length_bytes(ip)`, `3` and `8` for `length_bytes(s)`.

Likely cause: when an IPv4 argument matches a VARCHAR parameter, `FunctionParser.createFunction`
passes it on without a cast (it inserts one only for a STRING parameter), and
`IPv4Function.getVarcharA/getVarcharSize` throw. `SymbolFunction.getVarcharSize` also throws, which
`length_bytes()` calls.

Reproduced on master e4da5b4543.

<details>
<summary>Failing test</summary>

Add to `core/src/test/java/io/questdb/test/griffin/IPv4Test.java`:

```java
@Test
public void testIPv4AsVarcharOnlyArgument() throws Exception {
    // each call resolves to a VARCHAR overload for the IPv4 argument: length_bytes, json_extract and
    // arg_max have no STRING overload, the others win on total distance thanks to the VARCHAR column
    assertMemoryLeak(() -> {
        execute("CREATE TABLE t (ip IPv4, v VARCHAR, d DOUBLE)");
        execute("INSERT INTO t VALUES ('1.2.3.4', '1.2', 1.0), ('10.0.0.1', '10', 2.0), (NULL, NULL, 0.5)");
        assertQuery("SELECT length_bytes(ip) lb, starts_with(ip, v) sw, strpos(ip, v) sp, nullif(v, ip) ni, replace(ip, v, v) r FROM t")
                .noLeakCheck()
                .expectSize()
                .returns("""
                        lb\tsw\tsp\tni\tr
                        7\ttrue\t1\t1.2\t1.2.3.4
                        8\ttrue\t1\t10\t10.0.0.1
                        -1\tfalse\tnull\t\t
                        """);
        assertQuery("SELECT json_extract(ip, '$.a') je FROM t")
                .noLeakCheck()
                .expectSize()
                .returns("""
                        je
                        1.2.3.4
                        10.0.0.1

                        """);
        assertQuery("SELECT arg_max(ip, d) am FROM t")
                .noLeakCheck()
                .noRandomAccess()
                .expectSize()
                .returns("""
                        am
                        10.0.0.1
                        """);
    });
}
```

On master it fails with: `java.lang.UnsupportedOperationException at io.questdb.griffin.engine.functions.IPv4Function.getVarcharSize(IPv4Function.java:235)`

The SYMBOL case: `LengthFunctionFactoryTest#testSymbolLengthBytes` in `repro/test.patch` fails with
`java.lang.UnsupportedOperationException at io.questdb.griffin.engine.functions.SymbolFunction.getVarcharSize(SymbolFunction.java:261)`.

</details>

