The window forms of `percentile_disc` and `percentile_cont` that take an array of percentiles (`DOUBLE[]`) sort the whole partition. For a few percentiles over a large partition, this makes the query about 2x slower than it needs to be. The GROUP BY forms of the same functions select only the values they need and do not have this cost.

Example:

```sql
SELECT percentile_disc(x, ARRAY[0.1, 0.5, 0.9]) OVER () FROM t;
