### Cause

`preparePass2()` calls `DoubleSort.sort()` (O(n log n)) on every partition:

- `MultiPercentileDiscDoubleWindowFunctionFactory.java`, around lines 305 (`PARTITION BY`) and 469 (`OVER ()`)
- `MultiPercentileContDoubleWindowFunctionFactory.java`, around lines 306 (`PARTITION BY`) and 482 (`OVER ()`)

Only k order statistics are needed: one index per percentile for `disc`, and the floor and ceiling positions for `cont`. `DoubleSort.quickSelectMultiple()` already finds them, and the GROUP BY forms already use it (`MultiPercentileDiscDoubleGroupByFunction.getArray()`).

This was raised as the Critical point of the review on #6680 (https://github.com/questdb/questdb/pull/6680#issuecomment-6319398098). The PR merged without addressing it.

### Measurements

All numbers are on master `cebb783188`, using 4M random doubles and three percentiles (0.1, 0.5, 0.9). Each figure is the median of 7 runs in the same JVM.

| Measurement | master | with quickSelectMultiple (scratch patch) |
|---|---:|---:|
| `DoubleSort.sort` vs `quickSelectMultiple` on 4M values | 386.6 ms | 73.0 ms (5.3x faster) |
| `percentile_disc(x, ARRAY[0.1,0.5,0.9]) OVER ()` | 648.1 ms | 325.6 ms |
| `percentile_cont(x, ARRAY[0.1,0.5,0.9]) OVER ()` | 734.1 ms | 364.9 ms |
| `percentile_disc(x, ARRAY[0.1,0.5,0.9])` GROUP BY (reference) | 105.1 ms | 103.7 ms |

The scratch patch returns exactly the same results. The rest of the window query time is mostly pass 2 writing the result array into the record chain for every row.

